<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lint>
    <!--
      ktor-utils references java.lang.management from IntelliJ-debugger-only code
      (io.ktor.util.debug.IntellijIdeaDebugDetector) that never runs on Android.

      Scoped to the one artifact rather than baselined: a baseline entry pins the finding to the
      jar's cache path, which embeds the version and its hash, so every ktor bump unmatched the
      entry and failed the build twice over (stale LintBaselineFixed plus the re-fired error).
      Matching on the artifact name survives version bumps, and InvalidPackage stays live for
      every other dependency.
    -->
    <issue id="InvalidPackage">
        <ignore regexp="ktor-utils-jvm" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      The launcher rasters are PNG on purpose, and lint is right that WebP would be smaller: they
      cost about 26 KB more this way. They are not there for the launcher, which takes the adaptive
      icon in mipmap-anydpi and never reads them at all. They exist for Firebase App Distribution,
      which does not parse adaptive-icon XML and falls back to a generated monogram when it cannot
      find a flat raster it understands — see the launcher icon KDoc trail in git for what was
      already ruled out. WebP rasters shipped in three distributed releases and the monogram stayed,
      so the encoding is the remaining suspect and PNG is the wider-supported one.

      Scoped to these files rather than disabled outright, so ConvertToWebp keeps flagging every
      other image in the project, where the size argument does apply.
    -->
    <issue id="ConvertToWebp">
        <ignore regexp="mipmap-[^/]+/ic_launcher.*\.png" />
    </issue>
</lint>
